The first step is to settle on the method of autogrouping as a state
which can be on or off: will I introduce the concept of 'directives' for
this purpose, or can it be handled by data objects?

directive example:
        autogroup begin group1
        ; group modules etc defined here
        autogroup end group1
  pros:
    * one liner, easily understandable, unambiguous
    * easy to hard-code an inflexible handling of directives into the
      synth_file_reader data object.
  cons:
    * no parameters to control behaviour
    * no well designed and extendable directive handling infrastructure
      exists yet

data object example:
        autogroup ag1 begin group1 ag1
        ; group modules etc defined here
        autogroup ag2 end group1 ag2

  pros:
    * data_object infrastructure already exists
    * supports parameters to control behaviour
    * matches wcnt's existing syntax/definition
  cons:
    * behavioural divergence - something is happening outside of the
      data object definition
    * behavioural divergence - two data objects are used to create one
      thing/process
    * data objects require unique names, so the D_O username to begin
      autogrouping and the D_O username to end autogrouping cannot match.


