The group data object groups modules after their creation, it is not
possible for ambiguity over usernames to arise. Autogrouping will cause
modules to be grouped from their inception - this will introduce
potential for username ambiguity.

Given two modules clock1, and group1.clock1:

  * Using the group data object, the grouped module must be created
    and grouped before the non-grouped module, otherwise a name clash
    arises

  * Using autogrouping, group1.clock1 is grouped from the start (it will
    never exist as an ungrouped module), so order of creation is of no
    relevance to this example.

Given three modules clock1, group1.clock1 and sine1:

