BUT USAGE PROBLEMS PREVAIL
--------------------------

This problem isn't strictly tied to autogrouping. It's more the
inability to rename a group. Consider the entry points to a voice part.
To save time the user might decide to put the entry point modules into
their own file and group them. Then every voice part file that requires
entry points simply reads that file. But, if then a further file
utilizes multiple voice parts with each voice part file reading the
entry points, it's going to stop dead when as soon as the attempt to
create the second entry point group is encountered.

This could be worked around by the ability to rename the group. Okay so
the group data object is renamed, but then all the modules which are
members of that group must be renamed. Then all the connections for
those updated modules must also be updated too.

