========================
3) Nameless data objects
========================

As already mentioned, it can be a pain to create unique identifiers,
however several of the data_objects don't necessarily require a username
at all (with the exception of when using the exclude/include directives
of the synth_file_reader).

In wcnt, the username of a module or data object are also used in the
same way open & closing braces are used in programming languages.
Perhaps then, we could allow braces to be used instead and create
nameless data objects.

(Although I like square braces, not curly, if this idea gets
implemented).

Obviously if data objects are created without a name then they won't be
able to be specified for inclusion or exclusion by a synth_file_reader,
nor for parameter editing by a param_editor.

Some data objects (ie riff, wavfilein) require a name.

